Initiation: DNA polymerase binds to the replication site on the DNA and begins to synthesize a new DNA strand.
Elongation: DNA polymerase moves along the DNA template, reading the DNA sequence and synthesizing a complementary DNA molecule. The DNA molecule is complementary to the DNA template strand, with thymine (T) in the DNA sequence.
Termination: DNA polymerase reaches the end of the DNA template, and the replication process is terminated. The newly synthesized DNA strands are separated and can be used for replication in subsequent rounds.

