CO(g) + 1/2 O2(g) → CO2(g)

Since we are burning 3 moles of CO, we can multiply the equation by 3 to get the balanced equation for the reaction:

3 CO(g) + 3/2 O2(g) → 3 CO2(g)

Now, we can use the standard molar entropy values (S°) at 298 K:

S°(CO) = 135.6 J/mol·K
S°(O2) = 205.0 J/mol·K
S°(CO2) = 213.7 J/mol·K

Now, we can calculate the change in entropy (ΔS) using the formula:

ΔS = ΣnS°(products) - ΣnS°(reactants)

