6. If the starting material was achiral, the absolute configuration of the product can be determined by comparing the observed NOE patterns with those of known compounds or by performing X-ray crystallography.

7. If the reaction is not stereospecific, the product may be a mixture of diastereomers, which can be separated and analyzed separately to determine their configurations.

By following these steps, the configuration (R or S) of the chiral alcohol product formed from the reaction of a Grignard reagent with an acid chloride or ester can be experimentally determined using NMR spectroscopy.
