The fully ionized equation for the reaction is:

H(C₇H₅O₂) (s) + NaOH (aq) → Na(C₇H₅O₂) (aq) + H₂O (l)

In this equation, the sodium hydroxide (NaOH) donates a hydroxide ion (OH⁻) to the benzoic acid (H(C₇H₅O₂)), forming sodium benzoate (Na(C₇H₅O₂)) and water (H₂O).
