\[
\dfrac{(-\sin \alpha) \cdot \sin \alpha}{(-\sin \alpha) \cdot \cos \alpha} = \frac{\sin^2 \alpha}{\sin \alpha \cdot \cos \alpha} = \frac{\sin \alpha}{\cos \alpha} = \tan \alpha = -\dfrac{3}{4}.
