7. **Visualization**: Visualize the pressure coefficients and velocity profiles for each angle of attack to understand the flow characteristics and pressure distribution on the airfoil.

8. **Validation**: Validate the CFD results against experimental data or other validated CFD models to ensure the accuracy of the simulation.

By following these steps, the student can determine the critical angle of attack for flow separation and stall on the given airfoil using CFD simulation. The CFD simulation will provide valuable insights into the flow characteristics and pressure coefficients on the airfoil, which will help the student understand the underlying physics of flow separation and stall.
