<start_of_turn>model
","For an isothermal process (constant temperature), the work done by the gas is given by:
\[
W = nRT \ln \left( \frac{V_f}{V_i} \right)
\]
where:
- \( n = 2 \) moles (number of moles of gas)
- \( R = 8.314 \) J/mol·K (universal gas constant), converted to joules (since the pressure is in atm, the final answer will be in J)
- \( T = 300 \) K (temperature, assuming 1 atm = 1 atm and 1 atm = 1 atm, so \( T = \frac{2 \times 10^5 \text{ Pa}}{10^5 \text{ Pa/K}} = 2 \) atm = 2 atm, and \( 2 \times 10^5 \text{ Pa} = 2 \times 10^5 \text{ Pa} \))
- \( V_f = 8 \) L (final volume)
- \( V_i = 4 \) L (initial volume)

Substituting the values:
\[
W = 2 \times 8.314 \times 300 \ln \left( \frac{8}{4} \right)
\]
\[
W = 4988.4 \ln 2
\]
\[
W = 4988.4 \times 0.693
\]
\[
W \approx 3450 \text{ J}
\]

Thus, the work done by the gas during the expansion process is \(\boxed{3450 \text{ J}}\).",relevance,"# Task Description
