\]
The kinetic energy of the ball before the collision is:
\[
KE_{\text{initial}} = \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{in}}^2
\]
The kinetic energy of the ball after the collision is:
\[
KE_{\text{final}} = \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{out}}^2 = \frac{1}{2} m \left( \frac{1}{3} v_{\text{in}} \right)^2 = \frac{1}{2} m \left( \frac{1}{9} v_{\text{in}}^2 \right) = \frac{1}{9} \left( \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{in}}^2 \right)
\]
The fraction of kinetic energy lost is:
\[
\text{Fraction lost} = 1 - \frac{KE_{\text{final}}}{KE_{\text{initial}}} = 1 - \frac{\frac{1}{9} \left( \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{in}}^2 \right)}{\frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{in}}^2} = 1 - \frac{1}{9} = \frac{8}{9}
\]
