","The index of refraction \( n \) is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum \( v_{\text{vacuum}} \) to the speed of light in the medium \( v_{\text{medium}} \):
\[
n = \frac{v_{\text{vacuum}}}{v_{\text{medium}}}
\]
Given that the speed of light in the plastic is \( 0.680 \) times the speed of light in a vacuum, we have:
\[
v_{\text{medium}} = 0.680 \times v_{\text{vacuum}}
\]
Substituting this into the formula for the index of refraction:
\[
n = \frac{v_{\text{vacuum}}}{0.680 \times v_{\text{vacuum}}} = \frac{1}{0.680} \approx 1.46
\]
