   \]
   where:
   - \( F = 3600 \, \text{N} \) (gravitational force)
   - \( G = 1 \, \text{m/s}^2 \text{N m}^2 \text{kg}^2 \) (gravitational constant)
   - \( M = 4.48 \times 10^8 \, \text{kg} \) (mass of the Earth)
   - \( R \) (distance from the Earth to the satellite)

2. **Centripetal Acceleration Formula:**
   \[
   a = \frac{v^2}{R}
   \]
   where:
   - \( a = 9 \, \text{m/s}^2 \) (acceleration due to gravity)
   - \( v = 800 \, \text{m/s} \) (orbital velocity)
   - \( R \) (distance from the Earth to the satellite)

3. **Kinetic Energy Formula:**
   \[
   K = \frac{1}{2}mv^2
   \]
