\[
m = \frac{3600 \times (70888.89)^2}{9} = \frac{3600 \times 502000000}{9} \approx 200 \times 502000000 = 1004000000 \, \text{kg}
\]

**Step 3: Calculate the kinetic energy \( K \)**
\[
K = \frac{1}{2}mv^2 = \frac{1}{2} \times 1004000000 \times 800^2 = 502000000 \times 640000 = 3.2128 \times 10^{14} \, \text{J}
\]

**Final Answer:**
The kinetic energy of the satellite is \(\boxed{3.2128 \times 10^{14} \, \text{J}}\).
